  "summary": "Two lobed rotors turn in opposite directions inside a close-fitting case. They never touch each other or the case — timing gears in the gearbox keep them in phase — so the pump is gentle on shear-sensitive and particle-laden products and can run dry briefly. As the lobes separate at the inlet a void forms and fills; the liquid is carried around the outside of each rotor and expelled where the lobes re-mesh at the outlet. Widely used in food, beverage, pharmaceutical and wastewater sludge service; easy to clean in place.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – rotary",
    "configuration": "Rotary lobe, external timing gears, overhung rotors"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "lobes": 3,
    "profile": "Cycloidal (epicycloid tips / hypocycloid roots), non-contacting",
    "ports": "Bottom inlet, top outlet (reversible by changing rotation)",
    "seals": "Front-loading mechanical seals per shaft"
  },
